{%- unless include_assets == false -%}{% render 'cl-fixed-bundle-bootstrap' %}{%- endunless -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Optional param `personalized: false` -> plain native add-to-cart for bundles
  with NO plate/personalization (Canvas Wallet, Boonie, Backyard). It omits the
  Zepto personalizer mount and gives the button a distinct id so the personalizer
  JS (which intercepts #cl-fxb-form clicks) never touches it; the form POSTs the
  bundle variant natively and the cart-transform expands it into its components.
  Defaults to the personalized form so the 3-Hat bundle is unchanged.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="cl-fxb__scope cl-fxb__block" data-cl-fxb-scope data-cl-fxb-block="cta">
  {%- if personalized == false -%}
    {% form 'product', product, class: 'cl-fxb__form cl-fxb__form--plain' %}
      <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.id }}">
      <input type="hidden" name="quantity" value="1">
      <button type="submit" class="cl-fxb__cta" name="add"{% unless product.selected_or_first_available_variant.available %} disabled{% endunless %}>
        {% if product.selected_or_first_available_variant.available %}{{ cta_label | default: 'ADD BUNDLE TO CART' }} <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>{% else %}SOLD OUT{% endif %}
      </button>
    {% endform %}
  {%- else -%}
    {% form 'product', product, id: 'cl-fxb-form', class: 'cl-fxb__form' %}
      <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.id }}">
      <input type="hidden" name="quantity" value="1">
      {%- comment -%}
        The legacy PPLR/Zepto personalizer used to mount here via the
        `product-personalizer` class + `pplr-<id>` id. It hijacked the add-to-cart
        click and enforced its own "Custom Text Two required" rule, blocking every
        add (the optional second line could never be satisfied). The fixed-bundle
        ENGINE owns personalization now — it renders the state/fields/preview UI
        and writes every Zepto-contract line-item property itself — so PPLR is
        vestigial here. We keep an inert placeholder but remove every hook PPLR
        keys on (class/id/data-*) so it never initializes on this form again.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="cl-fxb__mount cl-fxb__zepto-hidden" aria-hidden="true" hidden></div>
      <button type="submit" class="cl-fxb__cta" name="add">
        {{ cta_label | default: 'CLAIM MY 3 HAT BUNDLE' }} <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </button>
    {% endform %}
    {%- comment -%}
      Zepto is unassigned from this product; the fixed-bundle engine owns its
      personalization fields and line-item properties. Disable native HTML5
      validation and route native submits (including Enter) through the engine
      button so nothing bypasses component expansion.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <script>
      (function () {
        var form = document.getElementById('cl-fxb-form');
        if (!form) return;
        form.setAttribute('novalidate', 'novalidate');
        form.addEventListener('submit', function (e) {
          e.preventDefault();
          var btn = form.querySelector('.cl-fxb__cta');
          if (btn) btn.click();
        });
      })();
    </script>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>
